hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18015","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Sulayman from Abu Tamimah from Duljah ibn Qays that al-Hakam al-Ghifari said to a man, or a man said to him: Do you remember when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade naqir and muqayyar, or one of them, and dubba and hantam. He said: Yes, and I bear witness to that. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: One of our companions narrated to me, he said: I heard Arim saying: Do you know why he was named Duljah. We said: No. He said: They set out with him by night to Makkah, then his mother placed him in the duljah at that time, so he was named Duljah."
"18016","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar: I said to Abu al-Shatha: They claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the flesh of donkeys. He said: O Amr, al-Bahr refused that, and he recited: Say: I find not in what was revealed to me forbidden to an eater who eats it. O Amr, al-Bahr refused that. Al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari used to say that, meaning he says: al-Bahr, Ibn Abbas, rejected that for us."
"18017","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from al-Taymi from Abu Tamimah from Duljah ibn Qays that a man said to al-Hakam al-Ghifari, or al-Hakam said to a man: Do you remember the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade naqir and muqayyar, or one of them, and dubba and hantam. Then he said: Yes, and I bear witness to that."
"18018","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Hajib from al-Hakam ibn Amr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man perform ablution from the leftover of a woman."
"18019","Mutamir narrated to us, he said: My father said: Abu Tamimah narrated to us from Dulajah ibn Qays that al-Hakam al-Ghifari said to a man once: Do you remember when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba and hantam and muqayyar and naqir. He said: And I bear witness, and he did not mention al-muqayyar, or he mentioned al-naqir, or he mentioned both together."
"18020","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us from Abu Hajib from al-Hakam al-Ghifari that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade performing ablution with her leftover, he does not know: with the leftover of her ablution or the leftover of her drink."
